# AppBids — Full Feature Overhaul Implementation Plan

## Overview

The existing codebase is a **Next.js 16 / React 19 / Tailwind v4 / Firebase / Stripe** app (the "pay-to-rank ad leaderboard with Plinko"). This plan overlays the 5-section feature request on top of the existing code with **minimal rework** — reusing all existing components and APIs where possible and adding new pages/components for new requirements.

---

## Architecture Summary (Existing)

| Layer | Tech |
|---|---|
| Framework | Next.js 16, App Router, TypeScript |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 + CSS custom properties |
| Database | Firebase Firestore |
| Payments | Stripe |
| Physics | Matter.js (Plinko canvas) |
| State/RT | 30s polling → will keep + add SSE/WebSocket placeholders |

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Plinko is currently a *bid multiplier* game** (not a standalone game with deposits). The new request asks for it to also be a standalone `/plinko` page where users can drop balls for real money. This requires adding a separate "Plinko balance" concept or reusing Stripe for per-drop purchases. **This plan will implement a standalone demo/free Plinko mode** on `/plinko` with responsible-gaming controls, and leave `// TODO: BACKEND — connect real-money plinko balance` comments where wiring is needed.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Live Auctions vs Ad Leaderboard**: The request frames the app as a "live auction" product (auction countdowns, product images, bidders count). The existing app is an *advertising leaderboard* (bids for ad rank). This plan **keeps the existing leaderboard as the "Live Auctions" section** and adds auction-style UX (countdowns, product images, bidder count) to the existing leaderboard cards. The data model will be extended with optional `endsAt` and `bidderCount` fields.

> [!WARNING]
> **Responsible Gaming (Plinko)** — KYC/age verification and self-exclusion must be enforced on the server side before real-money play. This plan adds all UI/UX surfaces (limits form, self-exclusion toggle, reality check pop-ups, helpline links) but **leaves server-side enforcement as `// TODO` comments** since the backend auth/KYC system is not yet built.

> [!CAUTION]
> **No breaking changes to existing API routes** — all existing `/api/ads`, `/api/plinko`, `/api/create-payment-intent` routes remain unchanged. New routes are additive.

